Alongside the materials chemistry, we work on shaping light with sub-wavelength
structure. Previous work includes achromatic metalens arrays for full-colour light-field
imaging, stress-induced 3D chiral fractal metasurfaces for broadband optical chirality, and
all-dielectric multiple-quantum-well metasurfaces that dramatically enhance second-harmonic
generation.

Increasingly these two threads meet: nanophotonic structuring is a way to get more out of thin,
imperfect absorbers.
